# Application workflow

Read tsrust.config.json and tsrust.api.json before changing paths or exposed APIs.
app/ contains native backend source; web/ is a normal user-owned React/Vite project
when selected. packages/api and app/generated-api are checked generated outputs.
Only explicitly selected operations are exposed. Read app/access.tsr: the greeting
is public; do not extend that policy to sensitive operations without implementing
the application's access controls. Never embed credentials in VITE_ variables.

Use tsrust check, tsrust test and tsrust format --check for backend changes.
Regenerate with tsrust api generate when contracts change and inspect the diff.
Do not hand-edit generated codecs or compatibility history to bypass validation.
Keep SDK package/API versioning and retained client compatibility deliberate.

Use ordinary package-manager commands in web. lib/api.ts and local components are
editable application code, not generated SDK output. Preserve owner edits and
lockfiles. Keep dependency upgrades explicit and run pnpm build afterward.
Check compiler, TypeScript and editor diagnostics; keep dev errors visible.

Run tsrust dev at the root and pnpm dev in web for development. Backend changes
rebuild through Tsrust; frontend changes use upstream Vite hot reload. Run API
generation explicitly after contract changes. Stop both owned dev processes when
finished. Do not publish packages, deploy or change signing trust without permission.
